# Only studios/vcut and its workspace dependencies ever need to be IN the image — this repo is a
# big multi-app monorepo (mobile native projects, other studios' asset-heavy content, Electron
# desktop resources) that the vcut.io web deploy has no use for. pnpm still needs every workspace
# package.json + the root lockfile to resolve installs correctly (pnpm discovers workspace members
# by scanning pnpm-workspace.yaml's globs against what's actually on disk, and a frozen-lockfile
# install fails if a member's directory is missing entirely) — but nothing else under those
# directories (node_modules, build output, native projects) is needed at all.
#
# Deliberately NOT using `**/node_modules`-style recursive globs — a real `fly deploy` against this
# exact file left apps/ at 486MB of a 561MB uploaded context despite that pattern being present,
# and flyctl's own build-context bundling has multiple open/history-of GitHub issues (superfly/
# flyctl#456, #3228) about .dockerignore patterns not being honored the same way Docker's own CLI
# honors them. Every pattern below is either a literal directory name or a single `*` one level
# deep — listed once per actual workspace member (packages/*, studios/*, apps/* per
# pnpm-workspace.yaml) rather than trusting a recursive wildcard to reach all of them.

node_modules
.git
.claude
.desktop
.vstudio
.vcut
.veasna-workspace

# packages/loom, packages/vicons, and packages/vcut are git submodules (see .gitmodules) — each
# has its OWN .git at that nested path, which the bare `.git` pattern above does NOT reach (dockerignore
# patterns without a leading `**/` only match at the context root). packages/loom and packages/vicons
# use the normal "absorbed" gitlink (a tiny pointer file, harmless either way), but packages/vcut/.git
# is a full nested repo directory — .git/hooks/*.sample ships files with permission bits that don't
# survive Go's archive/tar on Windows (`unknown file mode ?rwxr-xr-x`), which is what was actually
# breaking `fly deploy`'s context upload, not the size of anything.
packages/loom/.git
packages/vicons/.git
packages/vcut/.git

# packages/ai/src is a Windows junction pointing OUTSIDE this repo entirely (to a separate rixie/core
# checkout — see packages/ai's own workspace-symlink setup) — not a real directory, and reparse
# points like this are the actual root cause of the tar upload failing (`unknown file mode
# ?rwxr-xr-x`), not context size. Excluded outright: @veasnawt/ai isn't a studios/vcut dependency, so
# nothing here is needed for this build regardless.
packages/ai/src
packages/ai/node_modules
packages/analytics/node_modules
packages/auth/node_modules
packages/automation/node_modules
packages/database/node_modules
packages/editor/node_modules
packages/loom/node_modules
packages/storage/node_modules
packages/ui/node_modules
packages/universe/node_modules
packages/utils/node_modules
packages/vcut/node_modules
packages/vicons/node_modules
packages/vicons/dist

# studios/gamedev is itself a Windows junction pointing OUTSIDE this repo (to a separate loom-engine
# checkout) — same external-reparse-point hazard as packages/ai/src above, and equally irrelevant to
# studios/vcut's build.
studios/gamedev

studios/art/node_modules
studios/bp/node_modules
studios/games/node_modules
studios/language/node_modules
studios/music/node_modules
studios/settings/node_modules
studios/universe/node_modules
studios/vcut/node_modules
studios/vcut/.next
studios/vcut/dist
studios/vcut/build
studios/bp/.next
studios/universe/.next

# Native mobile/desktop projects — irrelevant to the web image, and apps/mobile's Android/iOS
# native folders in particular are large enough to make the Docker build context slow to send.
# Each app keeps its own package.json (pnpm's frozen-lockfile install needs it to confirm this
# workspace member still matches the lockfile) — everything actually heavy under it is named
# explicitly instead, deliberately avoiding a `dir/*` + `!dir/package.json` negation pair: that
# combination (wildcard exclude, then re-include one file) is the specific shape multiple flyctl
# .dockerignore bug reports call out as unreliable, on top of the recursive-glob issue above.
apps/desktop/node_modules
apps/desktop/build
apps/desktop/dist
apps/desktop/release
apps/desktop/resources
apps/desktop/.desktop
apps/vcut-desktop/node_modules
apps/vcut-desktop/build
apps/vcut-desktop/dist
apps/vcut-desktop/release
apps/vcut-desktop/resources
apps/mobile/android
apps/mobile/ios
apps/mobile/node_modules
apps/mobile/dist
apps/mobile/build

# Never let a stray local secret reach a Docker layer even if the build context isn't otherwise
# pruned to ignore it — Next's standalone tracer already double-checks this at build time (see
# apps/vcut-desktop/scripts/build-resources.mjs's own stray-.env guard) but that check runs on the
# TRACED output, not the raw build context, so this is the first line of defense.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
